    {
      "filename": "British Transport Police - Nissan Pathfinder.jpg",
      "title": "File:British Transport Police - Nissan Pathfinder.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/British_Transport_Police_-_Nissan_Pathfinder.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:British_Transport_Police_-_Nissan_Pathfinder.jpg",
      "width": 2517,
      "height": 1629,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "dave conner from Inverness, Scotland",
      "description": "BTP officers and their vehicle took part in the Parade through the City Centre, to Northern Meeting Park where this vehicle was photographed.\nThe City of Inverness held its Armed Forces Day Parade in conjunction with Inverness Highland Games on Saturday 24th July 2010. The Parade - from Eastgate in Inverness City Centre, through the city and past the Town House, over the Ness Bridge and along Ness Walk (where salute taken by the Lord Lieutenant and the Provost of Inverness) to the Games venue at the Northern Meeting Park - comprised 7 pipe bands, and past, present and cadet representatives of HM Armed Forces together with standards. \nThe Pipe Bands comprised:\n- IRBLS (Inverness Royal British Legion Scotland)\n- Northern Constabulary\n- Queens Own Highlanders Regimental Association\n- Nairn &amp; District\n- Forres\n- RAF Kinloss\n- Sutherland Caledonian\nThe Massed Pipes and Drums were led by Drum Major Neil Jamieson of Aberdeen. Universities OTC\n\nAlthough overcast, it was thankfully dry throughout the Parade, which was greatly enjoyed by the thousands who lined the route.",
      "dateCreated": "2010-07-24 13:58",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "inverness-wk",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gfhz",
      "mediumPath": "_m/g/f/h/z/inverness-wk/british-transport-police-nissa-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/g/f/h/z/inverness-wk/british-transport-police-nissa-small.webp"
